"""Reviewed current acoustic rerun, with old results kept in their own archive."""
from html import escape as e
import re
import json
from pathlib import Path
from s1_array_audio_view import render as audio_browser,case_button
from s1_acoustic_revision_view import render_measurements
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
LABELS={'headset_mix':'Headset mix','distant_01':'One distant microphone','beamformed_mdm8':'Eight-microphone beamformed audio'}
def render(t):
 d=json.loads((ROOT/'research/s1-revised-sweep/review.json').read_text());body='<style>#array-response-content,#ami-array-sweep,#context-elbow-analysis,#revised-question-audio,#revised-pilot-controls{scroll-margin-top:10rem}</style><header class="hero"><h1>Experiment progress</h1><p>Automatic speech recognition (ASR) produces a transcript. Word error rate (WER) measures transcription errors; answer content is checked separately below.</p></header><section class="section" id="summary"><ul class="brief">'+''.join('<li>'+e(s)+'</li>' for s in d['findings'])+'</ul><p><a href="#revised-question-audio">Revised questions</a> · <a href="#array-audio-demos">Audio demos</a> · <a href="#array-response-browser">Response ASR browser</a> · <a href="#ami-array-sweep">Figures 1–3: question ASR</a> · <a href="#array-response-content">Figure 4: response content</a> · <a href="#context-elbow-analysis">Interpretation</a></p><p>Published evidence snapshot: '+e(d['reviewed_utc'])+'.</p></section>'
 body+='<section class="section" id="revised-question-audio"><h2>The acoustic revision now covers the question bank</h2><ul><li>All 105 primary questions and six additional published AMI voice versions have revised question and insertion audio.</li><li>Original wording, insertion timing and source audio before and after each insertion are preserved.</li><li>All 123 microphone/context positions below are fresh replays with the accepted P01 revision to background sound, speech level and frequency balance.</li></ul><p><a href="experiments/question-audio.html">Listen to all revised questions</a> · <a href="research/question-acoustic-bank/review.json">Paired original/revised input ASR and processing details</a></p><p>Each question uses past-only acoustic calibration. Spectral equalization (EQ) adjusts frequency balance. Some bank clips use identity EQ because no earlier paired requester reference is available. Background that failed the first ASR screening is replaced with stationary noise matching a measured past quiet-frame spectrum and root-mean-square (RMS) audio level, avoiding replay of source words. These ASR-guided choices do not establish human naturalness. The accepted P01 input uses actual earlier room tone and is unchanged from the listening preview.</p></section>'
 body+='<section class="section" id="ami-array-sweep"><h2>Revised microphone comparisons across 41 context lengths</h2><p>The same P01 question is replayed after zero to 309.03 seconds of preceding TS3006c audio. Source boundaries, the native 480 ms packet loop, prompt, greedy decoding, untrimmed history and the 40-packet answer window (19.2 seconds) stay fixed. Thinker, Talker, MTP and Code2Wav run with S2 disabled. The caller enables the first response at the known question end. These are nested contexts for one question, with one response per position. Forty silent input packets define a 19.2-second packet-clock answer window; generated speech duration can differ, and the replay is unpaced. This is an accuracy test, not a real-time latency measurement.</p><p>The mono Headset mix, one raw distant channel (Array1-01), and the released mono eight-microphone beamformed signal (MDM8) keep their original context gains. The raw and beamformed gains are +16.52 dB and −6.00 dB. Each source channel now continues to the insertion boundary, without switching to a headset tail. Question speech is matched separately to each microphone condition; its level and EQ are baked into the WAV, with no additional runtime gain. Question packets are byte-identical across lengths within a condition, while their waveforms differ between conditions.</p><p><strong>AMI subset:</strong> these are selected question-bank meetings, not a named official ASR split. The original pilot uses mono Mix-Headset for TS3006c (scenario meeting) and EN2004a (non-scenario meeting). This three-signal sweep uses TS3006c only. The released MDM8 beamforming is offline and may use later-recording statistics. <a href="research/s1-array-sweep/recording-provenance.json">Recording provenance</a> · <a href="https://groups.inf.ed.ac.uk/ami/download/">Official signal documentation</a>.</p>'
 body+=t('All 41 contexts per signal were attempted; incomplete generations remain unscored. Response-content scoring requires complete reference evidence.',['Signal','Strict question-ASR passes','LLM complete spoken answers','Source-reviewed complete spoken answers'],[[e(s['label']),str(s['recognized'])+'/'+str(s['WER_scored']),str(s['judge_complete'])+'/'+str(s['judge_scored']),str(s['audited_complete'])+'/'+str(s['audited_scored'])] for s in d['summary']])
 body+=audio_browser(d)
 for num,(name,label) in enumerate(LABELS.items(),1):
  body+='<figure id="array-wer-'+name+'"><div style="overflow-x:auto" tabindex="0"><img src="research/s1-revised-sweep/asr-'+name+'.svg" alt="Revised '+e(label)+' question word error rate across all 41 preceding-audio lengths, with original-input comparison" style="width:100%;min-width:850px;background:white"></div><figcaption>Figure '+str(num)+'. '+e(label)+' question-ASR word error rate (WER) versus preceding-audio length. WER counts substituted, deleted and inserted words divided by the reference word count. Lower is better. These values use S1’s own recognized-question fields from the packet overlapping the cutoff through the first four post-question packets (1.92 seconds on the input clock), held fixed in both versions. Green requires WER at most 0.25 plus assistant, shared, folder, conceptual and design; this is a transcription criterion, not an answer-content score. Gaps denote failed recognition windows. The lighter dotted curve uses the preserved original input. <a href="research/s1-revised-sweep/asr-'+name+'.svg">SVG</a> · <a href="research/s1-revised-sweep/asr-'+name+'.png">PNG</a>.</figcaption></figure>'
 body+='<h3 id="array-response-content">Figure 4: evaluate the generated responses</h3><p>Independent Parakeet ASR transcribes the actual generated response WAV. The qualified local Qwen3-30B-A3B-Instruct-2507 judge checks whether the response states two source facts: the files were in the shared folder, and the particular file was the components-design PowerPoint. Both facts come from C’s statements; fact coverage here does not separately score speaker attribution. It scores each fact using the candidate answer alone, then checks material unsupported claims against source passages. It receives no microphone label, context length or question-ASR result. Codex separately reviews every eligible response transcript against the source. This is not an independent human rating.</p><p>The plotted fact score is the fraction of these two facts stated. Full correctness additionally requires no material unsupported claim. Only levels 30–40 contain all reference evidence; shorter contexts and failed responses have no correctness score. The LLM and source review differ on '+str(len(d['judge_disagreements']))+' eligible responses; both judgments remain visible. ASR errors can affect content scores.</p><figure><div style="overflow-x:auto" tabindex="0"><img src="research/s1-revised-sweep/response-content.svg" alt="Three panels of response-ASR fact coverage, with unsupported-claim flags and source-review corrections" style="width:100%;min-width:850px;background:white"></div><figcaption>Figure 4. LLM-scored facts in actual spoken responses. Red crosses mark LLM-flagged unsupported claims, open red squares mark additional source-review claims, and hollow diamonds mark fact-score corrections. Incomplete evidence is shaded and unscored. One response per position; no confidence interval or general robustness claim. <a href="research/s1-revised-sweep/response-content.svg">SVG</a> · <a href="research/s1-revised-sweep/response-content.png">PNG</a>.</figcaption></figure>'
 body+='<section id="context-elbow-analysis"><h3>What the revised results suggest</h3>'+''.join('<p>'+e(s)+'</p>' for s in d['interpretation'])
 body+=t('Descriptive question-recognition changes, not estimated memory-capacity thresholds.',['Signal','First WER above 0.25','Later WER ≤ 0.25 contexts','Last WER ≤ 0.25 context','Sustained higher-WER tail'],[[e(s['label']),s['first_WER_above_cutoff'],str(s['later_low_WER_contexts']),s['last_low_WER_context'],s['sustained_high_WER_tail']] for s in d['elbow_summary']])
 body+='<p>All answer-eligible contexts retain the same final reference fact at 136.44 seconds; the question begins at 309.21 seconds, a fixed 172.77-second gap. This experiment varies additional earlier context, not the delay after a fact. Level 40 additionally includes 74.89 seconds of initial recording silence. Multiple questions, repeated trials and controlled fact-to-question delays are needed for a defensible response-quality elbow.</p></section>'
 body+=render_measurements().replace('ASR job ', 'Original P01 input qualification, before this rerun: ASR job ')
 body+='<details id="array-sweep-examples"><summary>Every context length, response transcript, score and audio</summary>'
 for name,label in LABELS.items():
  rows=[r for r in d['cases'] if r['condition']==name];body+='<details><summary>'+e(label)+'</summary>'+t(label+' exact revised results.',['Level / earlier audio','Question WER','Actual response'],[[str(r['index'])+' / '+format(r['context_seconds'],'.2f')+' s',format(r['recognition']['WER'],'.3f') if r['WER_valid'] else 'N/A',case_button(r)] for r in rows])
  for r in rows:
   body+='<details id="sweep-'+r['id']+'"><summary>Level '+str(r['index'])+' · '+format(r['context_seconds'],'.2f')+' s</summary><p><strong>Question ASR:</strong> '+e(r.get('question_asr') or '(empty)')+'</p>'
   if r['response_valid']:
    body+='<audio controls preload="none" src="'+e(r['audio'])+'" aria-label="'+e(label)+' revised level '+str(r['index'])+' response"></audio><p><strong>Actual response ASR:</strong> '+e(r['spoken_transcript'] or '(empty)')+'</p><p><strong>Native intended text:</strong> '+e(r['speech_text'] or '(empty)')+'</p>'
    if r.get('source_audit'):body+='<p>'+e(r['source_audit']['reason'])+'</p>'
   else:body+='<p>Unscored execution: '+e(r.get('error') or r['status'])+'</p>'
   body+='</details>'
  body+='</details>'
 body+='</details><details id="response-judge-method"><summary>Judge qualification and exact evidence</summary><p>'+e(d['judge_qualification_note'])+'</p><p><a href="research/s1-revised-sweep/judge-results.json">Prompts, authored qualification checks and actual judgments</a> · <a href="research/s1-revised-sweep/review.json">Separate source review and all curve values</a> · <a href="research/s1-revised-sweep/curve-values.csv">CSV</a></p></details><p>'+e(d['resource_note'])+'</p><p>Each sweep worker uses one H100 SXM 80 GB, with all S1 components on GPU 0 and Parakeet on GPU 0 only after S1 exits. Workers use private services and fresh sessions. The later text judge uses one H100 SXM 80 GB for weights and KV, after all four sweep workers terminate. Bank checks use one L40S 48 GB with Parakeet only. Each of the two pilot-control jobs uses one RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell 96 GB, all S1 on GPU 0 followed by ASR; P03 remains excluded by the unchanged context-capacity limit. Dependencies cap the whole task at four simultaneous GPUs.</p><p><a href="study-progress-original-acoustics.html">Preserved original-input figures and responses</a> · <a href="research/s1-revised-sweep/manifest.json">Current checksums</a></p></section>'
 if any(r['job']=='1401019' and r['state']=='TIMEOUT' for r in d['accounting']['jobs']):
  body=body.replace('Each sweep worker uses one H100 SXM 80 GB, with all S1 components on GPU 0 and Parakeet on GPU 0 only after S1 exits.', 'Each native worker uses one H100 SXM 80 GB, with all S1 components on GPU 0. The time-limited worker’s saved responses are transcribed in a separate one-L40S 48 GB allocation; other native workers run Parakeet on GPU 0 after S1 exits. Only unfinished positions continue on independent one-H100 workers with unchanged inputs and model settings.').replace('after all four sweep workers terminate', 'after all required native workers terminate')
 body+='<details id="rerun-resources"><summary>GPU count, type, role and allocation cost for every job</summary><p>All allocated jobs use one GPU each. S1 components share logical GPU 0 within a job; independent response ASR follows after those components shut down, on the same GPU unless a separate recovery allocation is listed. Input-ASR checks and the text judge use separate allocations. Two superseded pending controls were canceled before GPU allocation. A parent worker can fail after one case hits the generation limit while preserving its other completed cases; neither parent completion nor failure determines answer correctness.</p>'
 body+=t('Parent-job allocation accounting. A zero allocated count means no GPU was consumed; hardware then describes the requested type.',['Job / state','Allocated GPUs / hardware','GPU role','Allocation seconds / GPU hours'],[[e(r['job']+' / '+r['state']),str(r['allocated_gpu_count'])+' / '+e(r['gpu_type_vram']),e(r['role']),str(r['elapsed_seconds'])+' / '+format(r['gpu_hours'],'.6f')] for r in d['accounting']['jobs']])
 body+='</details>'
 from s1_revised_controls_view import render as pilot_controls
 body+=pilot_controls(t)
 archive=ROOT/'study-progress-original-acoustics.html'
 if archive.exists():
  current=set(re.findall(r'\bid="([^"]+)"',body))|{'main','counts','checklist','software-checks','examples','reporting','appendix','retired-method','implementation','MathJax-script'};old=list(dict.fromkeys(re.findall(r'\bid="([^"]+)"',archive.read_text())))
  missing=[anchor for anchor in old if anchor not in current]
  body+='<details id="earlier-experiment-links"><summary>Earlier experiment controls and original-input details</summary><p>These compatibility links preserve earlier report fragments. Original results remain in their dated snapshot.</p>'
  for anchor in missing:body+='<p id="'+e(anchor)+'"><a href="study-progress-original-acoustics.html#'+e(anchor)+'">Earlier '+e(anchor.replace('-',' '))+'</a></p>'
  body+='</details>'
 return body
